# Restolution export (core purpose)

Inventaario’s main job is easy inventory input → a spreadsheet Restolution can read.

## Required column order (do not reorder)

| # | Header (exact) |
|---|---|
| 1 | Tuotekoodi / Product Code |
| 2 | Tuote / Product Name |
| 3 | Alkuvarasto / Beginning Inventory |
| 4 | Ostot / Purchases |
| 5 | Loppuvarasto / Ending Inventory |
| 6 | Ainekäyttö / Actual Usage |
| 7 | Tarve / Theoretical Need |
| 8 | Ero / Variance |
| 9 | Varastonkiertonopeus / Inventory Turnover |

Source of truth: `RESTOLUTION_FI_HEADERS` + `restolution` profile in `src/lib/export/profiles.ts`.
Default export/view profile is `restolution`.

## Formulas

- Ainekäyttö = Alkuvarasto + Ostot − Loppuvarasto
- Ero = Ainekäyttö − Tarve
- Varastonkiertonopeus = Ainekäyttö / ((Alku + Loppu) / 2) — **two decimal places**; only when usage > 0 (0 when usage is 0; "—" when usage < 0 or incomplete period)
- Incomplete period (no known Alkuvarasto and no Ostot): Ainekäyttö / Ero / Varastonkiertonopeus = "—" — do not treat missing opening as 0 and invent negative usage from ending stock alone

## Product code

Prefer `Product.productCode` (Restolution codes like `M1001`), then `Product.ean`. Do not drop Tuotekoodi from the export profile.

## Notes

- Do not add Päivämäärä / Yksikkö to the Restolution profile — they are not in the Restolution template.
- Other profiles (amounts, withPrice, nameQty) stay available for casual lists; Restolution stays first/default.
- Tarve may be 0 until meal-plan/covers wiring exists; keep the column.
